<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.12.7: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00258</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.12.7: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ade39f9d-c428-454c-bd0f-769f8fd785ff</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></para>
<para>In 1 - 2, find the equation of a line with given slope and \( y \)-intercept. Write the equation in slope-intercept form.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>slope 3 and \( y \)-intercept \( ( 0,5) \)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(y=5x+3\)</item>
  <item>\(y=3x+0\)</item>
  <item>\(y=3x+5\)</item>
  <item>\(y=0x+3\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \( y=3x+5 \)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-y_1&amp;=&amp;m(x-x_1)\\y-(5)&amp;=&amp;3(x-(0))\\y-5&amp;=&amp;3(x)\\y-5&amp;=&amp;3x\\y&amp;=&amp;3x+5\\&amp;&amp;\end{array}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>slope \(−3 \) and \( y \)-intercept \( (0,−1)\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(y=-x-3\)</item>
  <item>\(y=-3x-1\)</item>
  <item>\(y=-x+0\)</item>
  <item>\(y=0x-3\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\( y=-3x-1 \)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-y_1&amp;=&amp;m(x-x_1)\\y-(-1)&amp;=&amp;-3(x-(0))\\y+1&amp;=&amp;-3(x)\\y+1&amp;=&amp;-3x\\y&amp;=&amp;-3x-1\end{array}\)</para>
<para>In 3 - 4, choose the slope-intercept form of
  the equation of the line, shown in each graph. </para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/09a02347b18374d51af8598355f5cf5524859116"/></media></figure></item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(y=-3x+5\)</item>
  <item>\(y=5x-3\)</item>
  <item>\(y=-5x+3\)</item>
  <item>\(y=3x-5\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\( y=3x-5 \)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(1)-(-2)}{(2)-(1)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{1+2}{2-1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{3}{1}=3\end{array}\)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y−y_1&amp;=&amp;m(x−x_1)\\y−(−2)&amp;=&amp;3(x−(1))\\y+2&amp;=&amp;3(x−1)\\y+2&amp;=&amp;3x−3\\y&amp;=&amp;3x−5\end{array}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/eeae77b746d027b94298de1aaee697496e0d56a5"/></media></figure></item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(y=-2x+4\)</item>
  <item>\(y=2x+4\)</item>
  <item>\(y=\frac12x -4\)</item>
  <item>\(y=\frac12x+2\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\( y=-2x+4 \)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(4)-(0)}{(0)-(2)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{4-0}{0-2}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{4}{-2}&amp;=&amp;-2\end{array}\)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (0) &amp;=&amp; −2(x − (2))\\y &amp;=&amp; −2(x − 2)\\y &amp;=&amp; −2x + 4\end{array}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>Choose the equation of a line with the given
    slope and containing the given point that best represents the line in
    slope-intercept form.</item>
</list>
<para> \( m= -7 \), point \( (−1,−3) \)</para>
<list>
  <item>\(y=-7x-1\)</item>
  <item>\(y=-7x-3\)</item>
  <item>\(y=-3x+10\)</item>
  <item>\(y=-7x-10\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\( y=-7x-10 \)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (−3) &amp;=&amp; −7(x − (−1))\\y + 3 &amp;=&amp; −7(x + 1)\\y + 3 &amp;=&amp; −7x − 7\\y &amp;=&amp; −7x − 10\end{array}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>Choose the equation of a line containing the given points that best
    represents the line in slope-intercept form.</item>
</list>
<para>\((0,4)\) and \((2,−3)\)</para>
<list>
  <item>\(y=-\frac72x-3\)</item>
  <item>\(y=\frac72x+4\)</item>
  <item>\(y=-\frac27x+4\)</item>
  <item>\(y=-\frac72x+4\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(y=-\frac72x+4\)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(-3)-(4)}{(2)-(0)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{-3-4}{2-0}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{-7}{2}\end{array}\)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (4) &amp;=&amp; -\frac{7}{2}(x − (0))\\y − 4 &amp;=&amp; -\frac{7}{2}(x)\\y &amp;=&amp; -\frac{7}{2}x + 4\end{array}\)</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>Choose the equation of a line containing the given points
    that best represents the line in slope-intercept form.</item>
</list>
<para>\((3,−4)\) and \((5,−4)\)</para>
<list>
  <item>\(y=-4\)</item>
  <item>\(y=0\)</item>
  <item>\(x=2\)</item>
  <item>\(x=-2\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis> \(y=-4\)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(-4)-(-4)}{(5)-(3)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{-4+4}{5-3}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{0}{2}=0\end{array}\)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (−4) &amp;=&amp; 0(x − (3))\\y + 4 &amp;=&amp; 0(x − 3)\\y &amp;=&amp; −4\end{array}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which of the following equations is 
    \(y-5=3(x-2)\) written in standard form?
  </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>
    y=3x-1
  </item>
  <item>
    -3x+y = -1
  </item>
  <item>
    3x - y =1
  </item>
  <item>
    y=3x -11
  </item>
</list>

<para dir="ltr"><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 3x - y =1</para>
<para dir="ltr">\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-5&amp;=&amp;3(x-2)\\y-5&amp;=&amp;3x-6\\y-5+5&amp;=&amp;3x-6+5\\y&amp;=&amp;3x-1\\y-3x&amp;=&amp;3x-3x-1\\-3x +y&amp;=&amp;-1\\\frac{-3x}{ -1}+\frac{y}{-1}&amp;=&amp;{-1}{-1}\\3x - y &amp;=&amp;1\end{array}\)</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item>Write the equation of a line that contains the points \((–3,–1)\) and \((2,–2)\). Write the equation in point-slope form.</item>
</list>
<list>
    <item>\(y-2=3(x-4)\)</item>
    <item>\(y-4=-3(x+2)\)</item>
    <item>\(y+2=\frac13(x-4)\)</item>
    <item>\(y-4=3(x-2)\)</item>

</list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(y-2=3(x-4)\)</para>


<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item>Write the equation of a line that contains the points \((2,-3)\) and a slope of 8. Write the standard form.</item>
</list>
<list>
    <item>\(8x -y= -19\)</item>
    <item>\(8x +y= 19 \)</item>
    <item>\(8x -y= 19 \)</item>
    <item>\(19x +y= 8 \)</item>
</list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(8x -y= 19\)</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="11" type="enumerated">
  <item>Write the equation of a line that contains the points \((3, 1)\) and \((-1, 5)\).  Write the equation in standard form. </item>
</list>
<list>
    <item>\(x - y= 4\)</item>
    <item>\(x +y= 4\)</item>
    <item>\(-x +y= 4\)</item>
    <item>\(x +y= -4\)</item>
</list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x + y = 4\)</para></section>
